  "title": "Healthy Brain Network (HBN) EEG - Release 1",
  "description": "Release 1 of HBN-EEG, the EEG component of the Child Mind Institute Healthy Brain Network (HBN) project, organized in BIDS format. It includes EEG recordings and behavioral responses from 136 participants aged 5-21 performing six passive and active tasks: resting state, surround suppression, movie watching, contrast change detection, sequence learning, and symbol search. Events carry HED annotations, and the participants file includes quality control results and CBCL-derived psychopathology factors.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded while participants performed three passive tasks (resting state, surround suppression, movie watching) and three active tasks (contrast change detection, sequence learning, symbol search). Behavioral responses were merged into the events.tsv files with HED annotations. Minimal quality control checked for file integrity and required events, with results stored in participants.tsv.",
